      "body": "## Purpose\r\n\r\nSince read-only requests don't commit, we know that self-conditioning is unnecessary.\r\n\r\nApproximately ~3% improvement overall in structured queries.\r\n\r\n## Test Plan\r\n\r\n1. Unit tests: `tests/v1/sample/test_diffusion_gemma_reads.py` and\r\n   `tests/test_sampling_params.py -k \"diffusion or read\"`.\r\n2. Exact effect: count self-conditioning GEMMs per read in a torch-profiler\r\n   trace, before and after, over a dozen four-step reads.\r\n3. Read correctness on the branch build: grounded 33-field region battery,\r\n   coupled pinned reads at 1/4/8 steps, yes/no slot battery at four widths.\r\n4. Mixed batches: 32-way traffic of reads at several widths and step counts\r\n   beside open generations, checking failures and that the engine stays up.\r\n5. Generation regression: open-generation tok/s sweep at concurrency\r\n   1/4/8/16/32, engine restarted per arm, before and after.\r\n\r\n## Test Results\r\n\r\nGB10, NVFP4 checkpoint, Triton attention, text-only serving\r\n\r\n1. 64 passed, 9 deselected.\r\n2. Self-conditioning GEMMs per read 4.27 -> 3.00 (before: 11 reads, after:\r\n   12 reads). A read runs 3 to 5 denoise passes: early convergence, the cap,\r\n   or one pass the async scheduler queues before it sees the emit. The skip\r\n   covers the cap step and the overshoot pass. About 9 ms of a 330 ms read.\r\n3. Region battery 32/33 (baseline runs: 31 to 33). Coupled pins 22/24 at four\r\n   steps and 21/24 at eight (baseline runs: 20 to 24). Yes/no slots 7 or 8 of\r\n   8 per width, the one miss being the known borderline probe.\r\n4. 671 requests, 0 failed, engine answering afterwards, no tracebacks.\r\n5. Flat within run-to-run spread (variation here is normal run-to-run variance):\r\n\r\n   | concurrency | before tok/s | after tok/s |\r\n   |---|---|---|\r\n   | 1 | 79.2 | 73.2 |\r\n   | 4 | 128.4 | 132.8 |\r\n   | 8 | 171.1 | 177.6 |\r\n   | 16 | 190.4 | 201.0 |\r\n   | 32 | 198.3 | 199.5 |\r\n\r\n---\r\n<details>\r\n<summary> Essential Elements of an Effective PR Description Checklist </summary>\r\n\r\n- [x] The purpose of the PR, such as \"Fix some issue (link existing issues this PR will resolve)\".\r\n- [x] The test plan, such as providing test command.\r\n- [x] The test results, such as pasting the results comparison before and after, or e2e results\r\n- [ ] (Optional) The necessary documentation update, such as updating `supported_models.md` and `examples` for a new model.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n",
